{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/816487-where-worlds-merge","id":816487,"title":"Where worlds Merge","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-25T16:09:04-08:00","id":816487,"title":"Where worlds Merge","content":"Has anyone else wondered what would happen if multiple &quot;Umbral Reflections&quot; of the world were to overlap in the same place, where the mists, shroud, veil, gauntlet or what have you came down at the same time. <br /> <br /> For instance, what if in a spot where there were so few humans, but enough human acknowledgement of the places existence that there was almost no human &quot;disbelief&quot; de-magicing the area, but enough human imagination to join it to other worlds. Example:The north pole, the place where children's dreams of santa's workshop collect year round and thus join it to the dreaming(or the high-umbral reflection of earth if you're a mage), where there are thousands of miles of ancient untamed wilderness joining it to the werewolf pen-umbra(or middle-umbral reflection of earth), and a place that marks the graves of hundreds of brave explorers that died in int's cruel blizzards joining it with the shadowlands(low-umbral refection).<br /> <br /> In such a place how would said worlds interact with each other? how would their collective influence effect the &quot;Real&quot; area?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T13:54:32-08:00","id":817930,"title":"","content":"The only example of such a thing that I recall in the books was in the Week of Nightmares section of <i>Time of Thin Blood</i>. Apparently during the big fight between the Ravnos Antediluvian and the bodhisattvas someone opened a gateway to the Underworld, someone else opened one to the Middle Umbra, and they reacted with each other to also crack open the barrier to Yomi. It was my impression that all those portals being open was what made dropping spirit nukes result in the worldwide Avatar Swarm across all versions of the Gauntlet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T14:32:09-08:00","id":817964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/816487-where-worlds-merge?p=817930#post817930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only example of such a thing that I recall in the books was in the Week of Nightmares section of <i>Time of Thin Blood</i>. Apparently during the big fight between the Ravnos Antediluvian and the bodhisattvas someone opened a gateway to the Underworld, someone else opened one to the Middle Umbra, and they reacted with each other to also crack open the barrier to Yomi. It was my impression that all those portals being open was what made dropping spirit nukes result in the worldwide Avatar Swarm across all versions of the Gauntlet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I didn't mean it as literally tearing a hole in the gauntlet. I was more thinking along the lines of a cairn where the veil is not only thing that has thinned. Like an ancient burial ground in the wilderness functioning as both a cairn and a haunt as the barriers between the penumbra, shadowlands, and earth are thin(possibly resulting in a very confused wraith ending up in the middle umbra). <br /> <br /> Though I guess this wouldn't really come up except in crossovers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T08:44:17-08:00","id":819817,"title":"","content":"the dark tower series by stephen king I think ends up being a good example of what you are looking for. the universe is winding down and because of it the walls separating worlds has thinned to the point that in some areas it is completely non existent.<br /> <br /> I would run it just like your ideas above, travel through an area that resonates strongly with another plane of existence you may very well find yourself there instead of on earth. Walk through an ancient necropolis and find yourself in the shadowlands, travel through an untouched wilderness and maybe end up in pangea, navigate through the halls of a tech conglomerate and end up in some weaver realm, so on and so forth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}